This executable file is used to show a special picture at boot phase.

WHAT IT DOES?
=============
Show the second boot logo

HOW IT WAS BUILT?
==================
It needs the following library from AOSP:
1. libcutils.so
2. libutils.so
3. libc.so
4. libstdc++.so
5. libdl.so
6. liblog.so
7. libz.so

and the following libs from MediaTek:
1. libshowlogo.so

[Build Method]
mmm vendor/mediatek/proprietary/external/boot_logo_updater

HOW TO USE IT?
==============
Defined at init.rc and activated by init process.

###################

bit map text rendering :
Normal white 
bitmap[offset + 0] = (alpha * 255 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 0]) / 255;
bitmap[offset + 1] = (alpha * 255 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 1]) / 255;
bitmap[offset + 2] = (alpha * 255 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 2]) / 255;
 
Normal red 
bitmap[offset + 0] = (alpha * 255 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 0]) / 255; // Red
bitmap[offset + 1] = (alpha * 0   + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 1]) / 255; // Green
bitmap[offset + 2] = (alpha * 0   + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 2]) / 255; // Blue
 
Normal black
bitmap[offset + 0] = (alpha * 0 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 0]) / 255;
bitmap[offset + 1] = (alpha * 0 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 1]) / 255;
bitmap[offset + 2] = (alpha * 0 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 2]) / 255;
 
for Bold need to add this for loop (to thicker more increase < 2 to 3/4/5/6)
 
        if (glyph) {
for (int bold_offset = 0; bold_offset < 2; ++bold_offset) {  // Simulate bold
                for (int gy = 0; gy < h; ++gy) {
                    for (int gx = 0; gx < w; ++gx) {
                        int px = x + gx + xoff + bold_offset;
                         int py = y1 + baseline + gy + yoff;
                         if (px >= 0 && px < width && py >= 0 && py < height) {
                            int offset = py * stride + px * 3;
                            uint8_t alpha = glyph[gy * w + gx];
                            bitmap[offset + 0] = (alpha * 255 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 0]) / 255;
                            bitmap[offset + 1] = (alpha * 255 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 1]) / 255;
                            bitmap[offset + 2] = (alpha * 255 + (255 - alpha) * bitmap[offset + 2]) / 255;
                        }
                    }
                }
}}
 
 
 
 
and for Font size   
 
float scale = stbtt_ScaleForPixelHeight(&font, 40); 
